{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"germinable-cosey-vireo","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## The defect\n\n`scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py` — the deprecated-vocabulary guard wired into `make lint`\n— enumerates candidate files with a raw `os.walk` (`iter_repository_files`, ~line 144) filtered\nby a hand-maintained `EXCLUDED_DIRECTORY_NAMES` set (~line 23). That set covers `.git`, the\ntool caches, `.venv` and `node_modules`, but NOT `.claude/` or `bridge_state/`.\n\nBoth of those are gitignored (`.gitignore:49` and `.gitignore:14`) and both are created by\nnormal use of this repo: `make worktree` and the agent skills create `.claude/worktrees/<agent>/`,\nand the Jira bridge writes `bridge_state/snapshots/*.json`.\n\n## Measured in this checkout 2026-08-06\n\n    make lint  ->  47,312 \"deprecated vocabulary\" violations\n    violating files                       -> 1,393\n    of those that are git-tracked         -> 0\n\nEvery single violation is in a gitignored path — `.claude/worktrees/<agent>/docs/experiments/...`\n(an agent worktree carrying the repo's own frozen experiment corpora) and\n`bridge_state/snapshots/*.json`.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nCI never sees this because it does a fresh checkout with no worktrees and no bridge state. But\nthe pre-commit hook runs `make lint`, so any developer or agent who has ever created a worktree\nhas a permanently red commit gate for reasons unrelated to their change. The obvious escape is\n`git commit --no-verify`, which disables the whole gate — so a hand-maintained exclusion list\nthat drifts converts a quality gate into pressure to bypass quality gates.\n\nThe exclusion list is the root cause, not the two missing entries: it is a denylist over an\nopen-ended filesystem, so it will drift again the next time the repo grows a gitignored\ndirectory.\n\n## Approach\n\nDerive the candidate file list from git (`git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard`)\nso the guard considers exactly the files git would — tracked plus untracked-but-not-ignored —\nand `.gitignore` becomes the single source of truth for what is out of scope. Keep the existing\n`os.walk` as the fallback for a non-git-repo root (the guard's own tests run it against\nthrowaway `tmp_path` trees), and keep every existing curated exclusion (`docs/archive`,\n`docs/experiments`, the minified `editor.js`, symlinks) applied on top, so behaviour for\ntracked files is unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A violating phrase in a gitignored path does not fail the guard.\n- [ ] A violating phrase in a tracked (or untracked-but-not-ignored) file still fails the guard,\n      with the same path:line diagnostic as today.\n- [ ] The guard still works when the root is not a git repository (its own test suite depends on\n      this), and does not crash when `git` is absent.\n- [ ] The existing curated exclusions and the allowlist count-pin semantics are unchanged.\n- [ ] A test proves the gitignored-path case, RED before the fix.\n- [ ] `make lint` reports 0 vocabulary violations in a checkout that contains\n      `.claude/worktrees/` and `bridge_state/`.\n\n## Provenance\n\nFound while fixing bug a5f5 (`make worktree` builds its venv from ambient python3): creating a\nworktree is exactly the action that reproduces this.","id":"d5ae-5f4a-858f-431b","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"make lint is broken in any checkout with a worktree: the vocabulary guard walks gitignored paths"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786095474688828001,"uuid":"572b621b-e3e3-489b-9e55-2a8df93607a6"}